# Dogfood Task 1 · Drag-and-Drop File Upload

*paste-text form → drop a real file · auto-detect type · derive filename · 1–3 commits*

---

## Why

The current `/app/inbox` upload form is the single most off-putting thing about the demo. It asks the user to:
1. paste raw document text into a textarea
2. type a filename manually
3. pick one of 10 document types from a dropdown

For the same effort the user could just process the document themselves. The form actively contradicts the product story ("private AI workspace · drop your docs in"). And every potential client who tries the demo touches this form first — first impression is "this is a toy."

Three things are already true that make the fix small:
- `pdfplumber` parsing shipped in slice-4. The backend `POST /api/documents` already accepts a PDF UploadFile and extracts text server-side.
- The classifier analyzer auto-detects `classified_type` and the inbox already renders a `ClassifierBadge`. The user-supplied `type` field is effectively redundant.
- The pipeline runs analyzers based on `classified_type` falling back to `type`, so defaulting `type` to `"unknown"` and letting the classifier take over is a clean path.

This task removes the friction without touching the analyzer pipeline, the schema, or the deploy story.

---

## Scope

```
IN     frontend drop zone     /app/inbox sidebar Upload section
                                visible drop zone (dashed border · "Drop a PDF or text file here · or click to browse")
                                hidden <input type="file" accept=".pdf,.txt,application/pdf,text/plain"> for click-to-browse
                                drag events: dragenter/dragover/dragleave/drop · prevent default · highlight on dragover
                                single file at a time · multi-file deferred

       paste-text fallback   collapsed by default · "Or paste text…" link expands the existing textarea + filename input
                                kept for tiny corrections · not the primary path

       filename derived       File.name → uploadFilename · user does not type
                                paste-text fallback: auto-generate `pasted_<YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS>.txt` if user leaves blank

       type auto-detect       remove the <select> from the form entirely
                                api/client.ts uploadDocument signature: drop the `type` parameter
                                send `type="unknown"` to the API · classifier overwrites with classified_type
                                ClassifierBadge already renders the detected type in the inbox list

       backend default        app/api/documents.py: VALID_TYPES already includes "unknown"
                                no schema change · no migration · no analyzer change
                                file upload path already calls parse_pdf on application/pdf
                                add: text/plain content-type handling (read bytes → utf-8) for .txt drops

       loading + error UX     keep the existing uploading state · show selected filename + size before submit
                                show parse errors clearly (e.g. "Could not extract text · image-only PDF")
                                clear the drop zone after a successful upload

OUT    multi-file drop        one file per submit for now · multi-file is its own task
       progress bar           file is small · one spinner is enough · revisit if pilot complains
       any analyzer change    classifier handles type detection as it does today
       any DB migration       type column stays · "unknown" is already a valid value
       Romanian UI            tracked separately · do not start that in this task
       view-original-doc      tracked separately in ux.discoveries.md
```

---

## Acceptance

```
1  drop a PDF onto the drop zone in /app/inbox sidebar
   → file appears as "<filename> · <size> KB" before submit
   → click Submit
   → document is created with status="queued" · type="unknown"
   → within ~10s document moves to status="done"
   → ClassifierBadge in the inbox list shows the AI-detected type (not "Unknown")
   → no manual filename or type entry was needed at any step

2  drop a .txt file onto the drop zone
   → backend reads bytes as utf-8 · creates document with that text · pipeline runs

3  click "Or paste text…" → existing paste path still works (fallback)

4  drop an image-only PDF
   → backend creates document with status="not_supported_yet" + ocr_required audit event (existing behavior)
   → frontend shows a clear "Could not extract text from this PDF" message

5  drop the demo PDFs from apps/api/scripts/demo_pdfs/ one at a time
   → each one classifies correctly (matches what seed_demo.py declared as the type)

6  no manual document-type dropdown anywhere on the page

7  npm run check passes · no new svelte-check errors
```

---

## Files

```
EDIT   apps/web/src/routes/app/inbox/+page.svelte
        replace upload-form block: drop zone + hidden file input + collapsed paste fallback
        remove DOC_TYPES dropdown from form (the const can stay if used elsewhere · audit it)
        new state: uploadFile (File | null), uploadDragOver (bool), pasteFallbackOpen (bool)
        handleUpload reads uploadFile and posts via uploadDocument(file) OR uploadText path

EDIT   apps/web/src/lib/api/client.ts
        uploadDocument: drop `type` parameter
        accept either { file: File } OR { text: string, filename: string }
        send type="unknown" server-side · let backend + classifier do the rest

EDIT   apps/api/app/api/documents.py
        accept text/plain content-type alongside application/pdf
        for text/plain: file_bytes.decode("utf-8", errors="replace") → raw_text
        no other change · type="unknown" is already valid
```

